From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] venus: fail a Metal export without a heap

MoltenVK returns VK_SUCCESS and a NULL MTLHeap for memory it did not put
in a heap; the render server then crashed QEMU in CFRetain(NULL).

Upstream: not applicable (tap's Metal export).
Test: none automatic; the crash was seen with MoltenVK before the fix.

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
index 504b655..382eaf1 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -658,8 +658,9 @@ vkr_device_memory_export_blob(struct vkr_device_memory *mem,
          .handleType = handle_type,
       };
       VkResult ret = vk->GetMemoryMetalHandleEXT(mem->device->base.handle.device, &metal_info, &metal_heap);
-      if (ret != VK_SUCCESS) {
-         vkr_log("metal export failed (vk ret %d)", ret);
+      if (ret != VK_SUCCESS || !metal_heap) {
+         /* MoltenVK has a heap only with MVK_CONFIG_USE_MTLHEAP=1 */
+         vkr_log("metal export failed (vk ret %d, heap %p)", ret, (void *)metal_heap);
          return false;
       }
    } else {
